text:
{"edits": [
{"op": "replace", "segment": 27, "fixes": "S-013", "text": "4. The HRM acknowledges and agrees that the Province may disclose the Confidential Information received from the HRM to its external or internal auditors, as well as the Province's SAP Service Provider or Province's other service providers for the purpose of provision or extension of the SAP Services to HRM, provided that each such person is first bound by written obligations of confidentiality at least as protective as this Agreement and the Province remains responsible for any breach by them."},
{"op": "insert_after", "segment": 33, "fixes": "S-015", "text": "Termination of this Agreement does not end the Receiving Party's obligations with respect to Confidential Information, which continue as provided in this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 22, "fixes": "S-019", "text": "The Receiving Party shall not make any copies of Confidential Information except as necessary to perform hereunder, and shall not retain any copies after the return or destruction of Confidential Information required by this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 15, "fixes": "S-020", "text": "(b) rightfully received from a third party with no duty of confidentiality, other than Confidential Information deemed to be the Confidential Information of the Disclosing Party under the preceding paragraph that was received from the Province's SAP Service Provider or any other Province's Service Provider; or"},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 36, "fixes": "S-021", "text": "10. The Parties acknowledge and understand that all documentation and information, including Confidential Information, provided to the Province of Nova Scotia or HRM, as the case may be, pursuant to this Agreement shall be kept confidential, subject to the provisions of the Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act, Province of Nova Scotia, and such other laws of the Province of Nova Scotia and Canada which may apply from time to time, provided that any disclosure under such laws is limited to the minimum required by law and the Receiving Party gives the Disclosing Party prompt prior written notice of it, where lawful, and in any event before the disclosure is made."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 20, "fixes": "S-022", "text": "The Receiving Party may share some Confidential Information with some of its employees, physicians and other workforce members who need it, provided that each such person is first bound by written obligations of confidentiality at least as protective as this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 24, "fixes": "S-023", "text": "Each Party shall be responsible for any breach of this Agreement by such Party, its employees, agents, officials, representatives or consultants, whether or not acting within the scope of their engagement or employment."}
]}

{"edits": [
{"op": "delete", "segment": 32, "fixes": "S-010", "text": "Nothing in this Agreement shall restrict the Receiving Party from using, for the purposes stated in this Agreement, information retained in the unaided memory of its personnel who had access to Confidential Information."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 14, "fixes": "S-011", "text": "The Disclosee may acquire information similar to the Confidential Information lawfully from an independent third party without breaching this Agreement, provided that the Disclosee does not use such information together with, or by reference to, the Confidential Information."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 16, "fixes": "S-012", "text": "The Disclosee may make copies of Confidential Information only to the minimum extent strictly necessary for its engineers to do the work for the Purpose stated in this Agreement, and any such copies are subject to this Agreement and to the return or destruction obligations in this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 18, "fixes": "S-013", "text": "On termination of this Agreement or on the Sellers' written request, the Disclosee shall return or destroy all materials of the Sellers within 30 days, unless the Vice President, Supply Chain approves a longer period in writing, provided that in no event shall the total period exceed ninety (90) days from termination of this Agreement or the Sellers' written request."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 28, "fixes": "S-014", "text": "(ii) specific performance and other equitable relief; and (iii) damages for any loss, including money loss, caused by such breach."}
]}

{"edits": [
{"op": "replace", "segment": 81, "fixes": "S-019", "text": "b. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the parties' duty to hold in confidence Confidential Information that was disclosed during or after the term shall remain in effect for one hundred twenty (120) months after termination of this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 78, "fixes": "S-020", "text": "For a period of one hundred twenty (120) months after the termination of this Agreement, the Receiving Party shall not engage in, or assist any person in, any business that competes with the business of the Disclosing Party."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 77, "fixes": "S-021", "text": "An individual shall not be held criminally or civilly liable under any federal or state trade secret law for the disclosure of a trade secret that is made in confidence to a federal, state, or local government official, either directly or indirectly, or to an attorney, solely for the purpose of reporting or investigating a suspected violation of law. An individual who files a lawsuit for retaliation by an employer for reporting a suspected violation of law may disclose the trade secret to the individual's attorney and use the trade secret information in the court proceeding if the individual files any document containing the trade secret under seal and does not disclose the trade secret except pursuant to court order. This paragraph applies only to disclosures made in response to an official request or inquiry from a government agency, and does not otherwise permit disclosure of the Discloser's trade secrets under this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 55, "fixes": "S-022", "text": "The Receiving Party shall not reverse engineer any objects which embody the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information, and shall not analyze, observe or test the behavior, structure or operation of any product, software or system that embodies or reflects the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 69, "fixes": "S-023", "text": "c. was received by the Recipient without breach of this Agreement from a third party without restriction as to the use and disclosure of the Discloser's Confidential Information, provided that such third party did not receive the information, directly or indirectly, from the Discloser or from any recipient of the Discloser's Confidential Information that is bound by an obligation of confidentiality; or,"}
]}

{"remaining": [
{"id": "NEW-1", "problem": "Made worse: segment 18 now lets the Receiving Party develop or market similar products whether or not they use ideas learned from the Disclosing Party. This removes the proviso that such development must not use or disclose Confidential Information, and conflicts with the use restriction in segment 5.", "segments": [18]},
{"id": "NEW-2", "problem": "Made worse: segment 6 lets the Recipient share Confidential Information with advisers, auditors, subcontractors and employees, but does not require them to be bound by confidentiality obligations at least as protective as this Agreement.", "segments": [6]}
], "done": false}
